# Agent worktrees. Claude Code checks out git worktrees here, so this directory
# holds a whole second copy of the repo — evidence JSON, cargo snapshots and all.
# It is git-excluded, but Prettier walks the FILESYSTEM rather than the index, so
# without this line `pnpm check` fails locally for anyone with a worktree open
# while CI, which checks out clean, passes. A local gate that fails where the
# remote one passes trains you to ignore local failures, which is the same
# corrosion as a local gate that is weaker than CI — just pointing the other way.
.claude/worktrees/

# Markdown is hand-formatted here on purpose. Prettier reflows tables and
# rewrites emphasis markers, which buries real docs changes under churn — and
# this repo's docs are read by a grant reviewer, not just by us.
*.md

# Shaped by hand: the _README/_doNotWatch warnings are laid out to be read, and
# Prettier would collapse them.
evergreen.config.example.json

# Regenerated by `cargo test` on every run. Formatting these means Prettier and
# Cargo overwrite each other forever.
contracts/**/test_snapshots/

# Recorded RPC responses. These are kept byte-for-byte as the network returned
# them — see packages/core/test/fixtures/README.md. Reformatting one would
# defeat the point of having it.
packages/core/test/fixtures/

# Preserve recorded RPC responses and exported workflow logs byte-for-byte.
docs/evidence/

# Recorded scans and data generated from committed sources, rewritten by
# `apps/web/scripts/*`. Same reason as the core fixtures above: a recorded
# response is kept as it was produced, and formatting it means the formatter
# and the generator overwrite each other on every refresh.
apps/web/data/

# Build output. `apps/web/build.mjs` writes the dashboard here and Cloudflare
# Pages publishes this directory, so the files are committed — but they are
# generated, and reformatting them means Prettier and the build overwrite each
# other forever. The sources under `apps/web/src/` are formatted and checked.
apps/dashboard/public/
